Excel and PowerPoint downloads in the Environment Fund identity (#149, #145 Phase A), built in the browser from the
Markdown of a reply or document like the Word file of #135: Office Open XML in a stored ZIP, no new dependency.
- Excel (utils/efaiwXlsx.ts): one sheet per table, named after the heading above it.
  - A number (Western, Arabic-Indic or Persian digits; thousands separators; a percentage; a unit or currency; an
    accounting negative in parentheses) is stored as a number with its display format, grouped only when it was
    written grouped. Dates, codes with a leading zero and more than 15 digits stay text.
  - Header row in the EF palette, frozen, with a filter; columns sized to their text; Arabic sheets right to left;
    Tahoma.
- PowerPoint (utils/efaiwPptx.ts): 16:9 deck with the EF palette as its theme.
  - An EF-blue title slide from the first `#` (the paragraph under it is the subtitle; a reply's lead-in before it is
    left out); a slide per `##` (per `#` when there is no `##`); `---` ends a slide.
  - Bullets, numbered lists, sub-headings, quotes, code and tables (primary-blue header, banded rows).
  - What does not fit continues on the next slide, "(تابع)", and a long table repeats its header.
  - Real title placeholders; Arabic right to left, numbers kept left to right in their column's alignment; Tahoma.
- Menus (Chat/Messages/useDocumentDownloads.tsx):
  - «تنزيل» under a reply now offers Word, PowerPoint, Excel (when the reply has a table), PDF and Markdown.
  - The side panel's download button on a Markdown document opens the same menu, with the panel's text and edits.
  - The Markdown item keeps upstream's download; the menu portals into the fullscreen panel.
- Word (utils/efaiwDocx.ts): two schema errors that the Open XML SDK validator found and Word may repair on opening are
  fixed. `w:bidi` now comes after the page margins in the section, and the quote border is `w:left`, not `w:start`.
  `xmlEscape` is exported for the new files.

